#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:726
msgid ""
"A consumer that takes the tensor renames the capsule to \"used_dltensor\" "
"and takes over calling the deleter. A capsule collected still named "
"\"dltensor\" was nobody's responsibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:750
msgid ""
"Returns ``{\"driver\": int, \"device\": int, \"context\": int}`` -- the "
"``ze_driver_handle_t``, ``ze_device_handle_t`` and ``ze_context_handle_t`` "
"of VTK's one Level Zero context: one given to "
"``vtkDeviceArrayFactory.SetLevelZeroContext``, else that of the SYCL queue "
"Viskores runs on (VTK built with Viskores on Kokkos' SYCL backend, running "
"on a Level Zero device), else one VTK makes on the first Level Zero GPU. "
"``None`` when there is none of these: no Level Zero loader or GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:758
msgid ""
"A producer allocates in this context so that its ``kDLOneAPI`` tensors are "
"meaningful to VTK; see \"Context\" in the module documentation. The handles "
"belong to whoever made them: use them, do not destroy them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:771
msgid ""
"The tensor is 2-D, ``(number of tuples, number of components)``, which is "
"how the array is laid out. Single-component arrays are still 2-D with a "
"trailing 1; reshape on the consumer side if you want 1-D."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:775
msgid ""
"The array is kept alive for as long as the consumer holds the tensor, so it "
"is safe to drop every other reference to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:778
msgid ""
"*device_id* is the device the memory is on; by default VTK asks the vendor's "
"runtime (see \"Device ordinal\" above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:781
msgid ""
"With *versioned*, produces a v1.0 tensor in a \"dltensor_versioned\" capsule "
"instead of the legacy \"dltensor\" one. Consumers that ask for v1.0 need "
"this: over the legacy protocol NumPy cannot tell whether writing is safe, so "
"it marks the view read-only and then will not re-export it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:787
msgid ""
"Raises TypeError for a data type with no DLPack equivalent, and ValueError "
"for an array with no accessible memory -- implicit and computed arrays have "
"none to describe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:779
msgid ""
"Libraries call ``__dlpack__`` rather than taking a capsule directly, so "
"wrapping the array lets them consume it as they would any other array:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:782
msgid ""
"cupy.from_dlpack(DLPackArray(vtk_array))\n"
"torch.from_dlpack(DLPackArray(vtk_array))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.dlpack_support.md:779
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.dlpack_support.md:864
msgid "Initialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:808
msgid ""
"*source* may be a capsule or any object implementing ``__dlpack__`` -- a "
"CuPy array, a PyTorch tensor, a NumPy array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:811
msgid ""
"A 1-D tensor becomes a single-component array. A 2-D tensor becomes "
"``(tuples, components)``. Higher rank is rejected, since a vtkDataArray has "
"no way to represent it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:815
msgid ""
"The tensor is held open for as long as the returned array lives, so the "
"source can be dropped immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:815
msgid ""
"Asking for v1.0 first matters: NumPy refuses to export a read-only array "
"over the legacy protocol, because that protocol cannot say so. A producer "
"predating v1.0 raises TypeError, so fall back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:849
msgid ""
"Renaming the capsule is what marks it consumed: from here its own destructor "
"leaves it alone, and releasing it is this module's job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:864
msgid ""
"numpy.asarray() of this builds a view whose base is this object, so the "
"tensor stays open for exactly as long as anything is looking at the memory, "
"and is released once nothing is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:868
msgid ""
"The hold is this object's own lifetime, rather than the vtkMemoryDescriptor "
"release callback the device path uses. That callback is a ctypes trampoline "
"invoked from a C++ destructor, and a vtkObject can outlive Py_Finalize: "
"reaching for the GIL then crashes inside PyGILState_Ensure instead of "
"releasing anything. Python finalization runs while the interpreter is still "
"up, and the worst it can do is leak."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:875
msgid ""
"The array interface is what makes the view writable. Nothing here asks the "
"producer about mutability; dlpack_to_vtk has already read the read-only flag "
"off the capsule and refused if it was set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:885
msgid ""
"Host memory does not go through Viskores, and must not: plain VTK builds "
"have no vtkmDataArrayFactory, and host tensors are the common case. numpy is "
"only the vehicle -- numpy_to_vtk(deep=False) points a "
"vtkAOSDataArrayTemplate at the buffer and keeps the view alive -- and the "
"dtype comes from the same VTK type the device path derived, so the two agree "
"on what the tensor holds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/dlpack_support.py:899
msgid ""
"A factory being available says only that it was built for the memory, not "
"that it works on this machine: Viskores' is available wherever a device "
"adapter for the space was compiled in. So a factory that fails hands the "
"memory to the next one, its errors kept for the message should all fail."
msgstr ""
